(196704, 340885, 'Waves (melodic lounge) ', '海浪声中温柔守候，伴你入眠的浪漫电子小品。', 'https://usercontent.jamendo.com?type=album&id=29332&width=300&trackid=196704', '[00:06.28]Thank you.\n[00:47.64]Waves are rolling to the shore.\n[01:12.10]Stay with me a little longer.\n[01:17.82]Wait until the sun goes down.\n[01:54.78]Stay with me a little longer.\n[02:33.48]Fall asleep in my arms.\n[03:30.10]Waves are rolling to the shore.\n[03:34.38]Stay with me a little longer.\n[03:39.78]Wait until the sun goes down.\n[03:44.86]Fall asleep in my arms.\n[05:04.56]Fall asleep in my arms.\n', '/stream/196704'),
(2272813, 601347, 'Angel of Sorrow', '破碎天使在酒与泪中挣扎，渴望爱却只剩悲伤相伴。', 'https://usercontent.jamendo.com?type=album&id=612246&width=300&trackid=2272813', '[00:12.82]Sorrow breaks through, I hide but can’t explain,\n[00:15.94]Why do memories exist, just feeding pain?\n[00:18.82]They tear the wounds apart, they crush the tired soul,\n[00:21.46]Only wine inside my glass — the last thing I can hold.\n[00:24.94]Who is writing myths, defining what love means?\n[00:27.98]If it’s true, then where’s the angel in my dreams?\n[00:30.98]The one who cuts through grief and binds two hearts as one,\n[00:34.18]Why am I so lonely, God, what have I done?\n[00:37.14]If this is just a dream, then where’s the morning light?\n[00:40.30]And how to know the moment when to wake feels right?\n[00:43.38]But life won’t sleep, it throws us under blades,\n[00:46.44]No, I’m not afraid — I’m tired of these shades.\n[00:49.60]One day I might fall down, destroyed by love’s decree,\n[00:52.66]But something whispers deep inside: don’t quit, just breathe.\n[00:55.88]I live, enjoying what’s still left for me,\n[00:58.64]Just a glass, some wine, and sorrow’s company.\n[01:03.90]Angels never dream at night, I realize,\n[01:10.12]Angels never drown in grief, but here I cry.\n[01:15.84]I would spread my wings to fly, but they’ve been stolen,\n[01:22.10]I asked: “Who took them, why?” — but all was silent.\n[01:28.80]Angels never dream at night, I realize,\n[01:34.62]Angels never drown in grief, but here I cry.\n[01:41.00]I would spread my wings to fly, but they’ve been stolen,\n[01:47.08]Still I’m an angel, just broken, sorrow-laden.\n[01:55.66]How I longed for love to give me back my wings,\n[01:58.24]To breathe the purest air — but dust is all it brings.\n[02:01.36]I hide my tears in blankets so no one can see,\n[02:04.24]Not from sorrow, but from love that abandoned me.\n[02:07.30]Every day, believe me, I get lost in hope,\n[02:10.66]While love avoids my path — a cruel, endless joke.\n[02:13.80]How can I force my heart to stop, to not believe?\n[02:16.82]The fire’s drowned in liquor, but your shadow never leaves.\n[02:19.98]Lord, I beg You, please just help me to forget,\n[02:23.10]But prayer’s all that’s left — what else is there to get?\n[02:26.04]Who can truly understand, and even if they could,\n[02:29.24]It’s a war of love, a vendetta carved in blood.\n[02:32.28]My heart feels pierced by daggers, shattered deep inside,\n[02:35.62]And all that once existed, crossed out, left behind.\n[02:38.62]I live, enjoying what’s still left for me,\n[02:41.48]Just a glass, some wine, and sorrow’s company.\n', '/stream/2272813'),
