(1820439, 438603, 'Revolution', '一首怀旧民谣，追忆青春革命与逝去时光。', 'https://usercontent.jamendo.com?type=album&id=198495&width=300&trackid=1820439', '[00:18.48]sunlight through the leaves\n[00:20.12]afternoons, willow trees\n[00:23.00]endless moments and evenings\n[00:25.14]before the internet\n[00:28.84]kids were hiding cigarrettes\n[00:30.98]sitting in the field reading\n[00:34.88]i guess it\'s half nostalgia\n[00:38.02]but who\'s judging us today\n[00:40.22]when the images are here to stay\n[00:44.70]we used to talk about a revolution\n[00:48.34]sharing images and illusions i\n[00:53.44]on the roof with a pipe and writing\n[01:04.96]grassy wooden house\n[01:06.18]poetry, no applause\n[01:08.54]right until we two were banished\n[01:13.28]my favourite novel was\n[01:14.92]flight to afar just because\n[01:17.46]i had this dream that i would vanish\n[01:22.16]i guess it\'s half nostalgia\n[01:24.60]but who\'s judging us today?\n[01:26.84]and it all has been so long ago\n[01:30.12]we used to talk about a revolution\n[01:34.46]sharing images and illusions i\n[01:39.66]on the roof with a pipe and writing\n[01:43.76]invisible to the world we\'re fighting\n[01:48.36]i guess life got in the way\n[01:53.00]lead us both astray\n[01:56.74]or it\'s just the way the story goes\n[02:00.32]we used to talk about a revolution\n[02:02.66]sharing images and illusions i\n[02:02.76]on the roof with a pipe and writing\n[02:02.77]irrelevant to the world we\'re fighting\n[02:49.26]yes we talked of a revolution\n[02:53.84]whatever happened to you i am wondering\n[02:58.92]some might say it\'ll get easier\n[03:02.08]it\'ll be easier\n', '/stream/1820439'),
(2330818, 490580, 'Heartbeat', '温柔灵魂民谣，诉说守候与陪伴的深情告白。', 'https://usercontent.jamendo.com?type=album&id=640502&width=300&trackid=2330818', '[00:22.10]Thank you.\n[00:42.94]You\'re never walking alone here.\n[00:47.28]I\'ll be there waiting at home.\n[00:51.78]You\'re never walking alone here.\n[00:59.00]I\'ll be there waiting for you, baby.\n[01:29.53]You\'re never walking alone here.\n[01:35.69]Take me right back to the start of the day.\n[01:40.68]Take me back where we belong.\n[02:27.63]You\'re never walking alone.\n[02:33.08]Yeah.\n[02:33.80]I\'ll be there waiting at home.\n[02:38.26]You\'re never walking alone.\n[02:43.18]Yeah.\n[02:44.84]I\'ll be there waiting for you, baby.\n', '/stream/2330818'),
(2251031, 597558, 'Sorry in the Backseat (Alt Version)', '后座醒来追忆昨夜，迷失中追寻逃离的狗。', 'https://usercontent.jamendo.com?type=album&id=602092&width=300&trackid=2251031', '[00:05.42]Sorry in the Backseat-\n[00:05.43]I woke sorry, in the backseat\n[00:10.90]Of last night’s joy\n[00:12.60]Ridden car.\n[00:16.90]Recall faces,\n[00:19.02]In low-lit places\n[00:22.52]Wonder where they are.\n[00:30.12]Slip under memory’s skin,\n[00:31.84]Slide off the picture, facing.\n[00:36.10]Got the perfect scent of glue\n[00:38.18]But the dog ran… so I am chasing.\n[00:42.14]Enter a store\n[00:43.48]Where I thought I might be.\n[00:45.32]Salesman asked\n[00:46.58]Whether he could help me.\n[00:48.00]I don’t know what I’m looking for…\n[00:50.30]Probably not even in this store.\n[00:53.94]He looks right through me…\n[00:56.56]Outside: we see a young man,\n[00:59.76]Tyin\' a line to a chartered boat,\n[01:02.86]Slips on the tails\n[01:04.30]Of a big man’s coat.\n[01:06.58]My dog flees oppression…\n[01:10.08]And cautious procession...\n[01:12.70]See him, vanish\n[01:15.48]Past the waiting, crowd\n[01:22.28]Steam on the road,\n[01:25.12]Powder in my shoe\n[01:26.36]If the sky was a screen,\n[01:29.96]I just walk right through...\n[01:33.94]I woke sorry, in the backseat\n[01:39.88]Of last night’s joy\n[01:41.50]Ridden car.\n[01:45.86]Recall faces,\n[01:48.78]In low-lit places\n[01:50.64]Wonder where they are.\n[01:57.81]Never had the picture straight, and\n[02:00.05]When the dog ran… I was chasin’.\n[02:03.65]Where he’s going, could never define.\n[02:05.93]Just kept moving… so I stayed behind.\n[02:09.89]Woke sorry, in the backseat\n[02:13.73]Of last night’s joy\n[02:15.35]Sorry in the backseat…\n[02:22.08]Woke sorry in the backseat\n[02:25.79]Of last night’s joy\n[02:28.41]Ridden car.\n[02:32.05]Sorry in the backseat…\n[02:37.79]© & ℗ 2025 J. Marlow / So Said Mende. All rights reserved.\n', '/stream/2251031'),
