(1243456, 476284, 'Blu cobalto (Non c\'é) FIL', '意大利语流行民谣，诉说告别与不舍的忧郁情感。', 'https://usercontent.jamendo.com?type=album&id=211688&width=300&trackid=1243456', '[00:10.64]Blu cobalto (Non c’è)\n[00:10.65]arrangiamenti di Luca Annessi\n[00:10.66]Ho deciso di finirla qui\n[00:18.20]E mettere un punto a tutto questo disordine\n[00:27.58]Ho deciso di concedermi un attimo!\n[00:40.20]Per capire cosa significa scegliere\n[00:47.74]E tu che hai scelto me!\n[00:52.68]Tra tutti quegli sguardi pieni d’amore senza conoscermi!\n[01:02.72]Con i tuoi occhi di quel triste blu cobalto\n[01:08.70]Che nascondevano più di una semplice nostalgia!\n[01:20.46]Non c’è quel secondo in cui ho dubitato di noi\n[01:30.48]Non c’è nemmeno un paio d’ali, che mi avrebbe portato via\n[01:42.72]Ma ora sono qui disperso tra le maree di questo lampo improvviso\n[01:56.08]E devo andare!\n[02:00.20]E tu che hai mosso le\n[02:02.28]Corde più profonde dei miei battiti senza ferirmi mai\n[02:12.08]Chiedendomi se fosse il destino o il caso\n[02:18.96]Che mi ha allungato le tue mani in questa tempesta!\n[02:30.54]Non c’è quel secondo in cui ho dubitato di noi\n[02:40.46]Non c’è nemmeno un paio d’ali, che mi avrebbe portato via\n[02:52.70]Ma ora sono qui disperso tra le maree di questo lampo improvviso\n[03:06.06]E devo andare!\n[03:27.82]Devo andare!  Io!  Devo andare!\n', '/stream/1243456'),
(1635094, 512352, 'Charlie II', '慵懒独立民谣，讲述派对迟到的鳄鱼查理。', 'https://usercontent.jamendo.com?type=album&id=183856&width=300&trackid=1635094', '[00:05.80]Everybody wants it\n[00:06.78]Everybody needs it\n[00:09.50]But you’re showing up late to the party\n[00:11.64]Everybody come on\n[00:14.14]Everybody wants it\n[00:17.02]Everybody needs it\n[00:19.08]But you’re showing up late to the party\n[00:21.92]Everybody come on\n[00:24.14]Charlie you’re an alligator\n[00:29.10]Don’t leave me hanging after school\n[00:31.54]Show me what your teeth can do\n[00:34.10]Riding down the escalator\n[00:39.10]Saw you on the evening news\n[00:41.50]Black and white and red all over\n[00:44.24]Because of an aggressive alligator\n[00:46.02]That investigators say was at least\n[00:47.94]ten to eleven feet long\n[00:48.88]Everybody wants it\n[00:51.32]Everybody needs it\n[00:53.54]But you’re showing up late to the party\n[00:55.78]Everybody come on\n[00:58.24]Everybody wants it\n[01:01.06]Everybody needs it\n[01:03.36]But you’re showing up late to the party\n[01:05.54]Everybody come on\n[01:08.16]Charlie you know what you’re doing\n[01:13.48]Creeping round your mama’s house\n[01:15.82]Getting stoned and sneaking out\n[01:18.26]Babe you know the town is burning\n[01:23.32]What the hell you gonna do\n[01:25.48]No one’s ever trusted you\n[01:29.72]Is it getting harder now?\n[01:32.44]Is it getting harder?\n[01:37.84]Everybody wants it\n[01:39.82]Everybody needs it\n[01:42.32]But you’re showing up late to the party\n[01:44.70]Everybody come on\n[01:47.22]Everybody wants it\n[01:50.02]Everybody needs it\n[01:52.22]But you’re showing up late to the party\n[01:54.52]Everybody come on\n[01:57.30]Everybody wants it\n[01:57.40]Everybody needs it\n[01:57.41]But you’re showing up late to the party\n[01:57.42]Everybody come on\n[01:57.43]Everybody wants it\n[01:58.78]Everybody needs it\n[02:31.40]But you’re showing up late to the party\n[02:34.28]Everybody come on\n', '/stream/1635094'),
(2253625, 597558, 'Platform 3', '十九岁地铁站台的青春离别，回望旧日恋情的忧郁民谣。', 'https://usercontent.jamendo.com?type=album&id=603144&width=300&trackid=2253625', '[00:20.30]Platform 3\n[00:20.31]We were nineteen\n[00:24.98]Threading the subway\n[00:29.59]Bewildered\n[00:33.04]Puffed and stray\n[00:36.95]Retaining the artificial light\n[00:42.21]With nowhere to stay\n[00:45.85]In our orbit\n[00:47.75]Or under your sway\n[00:53.77]Time’s on fire\n[00:57.85]Behind your eyes\n[01:00.05]The Spark I knew\n[01:04.71]Is leaving on an impulse\n[01:08.57]I felt…\n[01:10.19]Unprepared\n[01:14.79]In the trade winds\n[01:18.95]And the engine’s calm\n[01:23.03]In a slow spin\n[01:27.15]Of your restless mind\n[01:30.75]Beneath the undecided sky\n[01:35.09]Tough as early spring...\n[01:39.43]If loves a monkey on your back\n[01:43.53]Then I’m a train slipping off the track\n[02:01.73]Just a kid\n[02:05.67]In a subway\n[02:10.25]Bewildered\n[02:13.17]Falling outa your gravity...\n[02:16.15]I still see you\n[02:20.15]At the far end of Platform 3\n[02:24.15]Watching trains like they owed you something\n[02:28.17]Now when I walk that line home\n[02:31.67]I still check the underpass\n[02:37.65]Just in case\n[02:40.37]You’re also looking back\n[02:42.99]Said same time\n[02:51.81]Next year\n[02:54.33]Doubt either of us came\n[02:58.31]And we knew\n[03:00.31]Some things\n[03:02.39]Only live once\n[03:04.35]Like that\n[03:05.47]Unprepared\n[03:10.37]In the trade winds\n[03:14.39]And the engine’s calm\n[03:18.41]In a slow spin\n[03:22.37]Of your restless mind\n[03:25.95]Beneath the undecided sky\n[03:30.23]Tough as early spring\n[03:33.55]One last look\n[03:41.49]You didn’t think I’d catch\n[03:46.45]And then you weren’t there\n[03:49.87]With all that noise\n[03:51.89]And none of the direction home\n[03:56.23]In a strong wind\n[04:06.89]In a slow spin\n[04:13.87]In the early spring\n[04:21.93]In the early spring\n', '/stream/2253625'),
(1693791, 522305, 'Night Star', '梦幻电子情歌，如坠落地面的夜星般浪漫治愈。', 'https://usercontent.jamendo.com?type=album&id=362111&width=300&trackid=1693791', '[00:02.48]Once upin a time I had a dream,\n[00:06.66]And that dream was about you.\n[00:50.40]First time I saw you,\n[00:50.41]Felt like a dream.\n[00:50.42]Noone else like you.\n[00:50.43]Your smile,\n[00:50.44]So enigmatic.\n[00:51.94]And your eyes,\n[00:52.20]Shining bright...\n[00:58.66]Like a ningt star,\n[02:25.58]Fallen to the Earth.\n', '/stream/1693791'),
